You will create a JSON and XML version of data. this data could be read from an Internet application, API (Application Program Interface) or other data sources. then you will access that data within a Python program. This program should display the data accessed and then prompt the user repeatidly for a book title and display the title, author and year published. Display a message if the book title was not found. 
Steps:
1. Create a JSON file. Add up to 10 books into the file. 
2. Write a Python program to access and read the JSON file and display its contents. (Load the file into a Python structure).
3. Write a loop to repeatedly prompt the user for a book title. 
4. Search the file for the title. If found display the title, author and year published. 
5. If title is not found in the data, display the title and a "title not found" message.
6. Develop the same steps but utilize XML instead of JSON.  
